    "narrative": "With the Zurich Zebras facing a light schedule today, the focus shifts to maximizing efficiency from our active roster. **Christian Yelich** earns the highest mark of the day with a 55.03 score, anchored by a favorable matchup against Rasmussen and a prime #3 spot in the order. His dynamic platoon advantage against a right-handed arm provides a 13% boost to his base projection, making him our most reliable asset for AVG and R output. **Junior Caminero** follows with a 52.05 score; while he faces a tougher challenge against Henderson, the #4 slot and his current recency hot streak keep him firmly in the \"Marginal-to-Strong\" transition zone. We are closely monitoring the lineup pending status for both, but their current projections suggest they are the only viable options given our limited active player pool.\n\nBeyond the starters, our depth remains largely stagnant today due to scheduled off-days for high-impact contributors like **Yordan Alvarez** and **Trea Turner**. The decision to keep **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Caleb Durbin** on the bench was purely tactical, as the lack of scheduled games for their respective clubs removed them from consideration entirely. Among those not currently slated to start, **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Colt Keith**, and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** remain on standby, but without an active contest, we are preserving our game caps for the upcoming series. We continue to track secondary prospects like **Carson Benge**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Josh Smith**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez**, ensuring that any shifts in weather or last-minute lineup changes don't catch us off guard as we aim to protect our narrow margins in the SB category.",
